## ✅ Function: Decode All 8 Channels from 24-byte SPI Frame

Add this to your `main.c` or a separate ADC utility file:

```c
#include <stdint.h>

#define NUM_CHANNELS 8

// Function to decode 24-bit signed value from 3 bytes
int32_t decode_24bit(uint8_t *data)
{
    int32_t val = ((int32_t)data[0] << 16) | ((int32_t)data[1] << 8) | data[2];

    // Sign-extend 24-bit to 32-bit if negative
    if (val & 0x800000)
        val |= 0xFF000000;

    return val;
}

// Function to decode all 8 channels
void decode_all_channels(uint8_t *rx_buf, int32_t *ch_values)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < NUM_CHANNELS; i++)
    {
        ch_values[i] = decode_24bit(&rx_buf[i * 3]);
    }
}
```

---

## 🧪 Example Usage in `main.c`

```c
uint8_t rx_buf[24];             // Received SPI buffer (3 bytes × 8 channels)
int32_t ch_values[8];           // Decoded values for all 8 channels

// After SPI receive
ADS131_Read(&hspi1, rx_buf);    // Read 24 bytes from SPI
decode_all_channels(rx_buf, ch_values);

// Print all channels
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++)
{
    char msg[64];
    snprintf(msg, sizeof(msg), "ADC1_CH%d: %ld\r\n", i + 1, ch_values[i]);
    print_uart(msg);
}
```

